.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd July 30, 2026
.Dt LIBLOGCMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm logcmp_client_open ,
.Nm logcmp_log ,
.Nm logcmp_flush ,
.Nm logcmp_stats ,
.Nm logcmp_client_close
.Nd structured capability-component logging client
.Sh LIBRARY
.Li liblogcmp
.Pq Fl llogcmp
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In logcmp.h
.Ft int
.Fn logcmp_client_open "struct logcmp_client **client"
.Ft int
.Fn logcmp_log "struct logcmp_client *client" "uint32_t severity" "const char *message" "const char *fields"
.Ft int
.Fn logcmp_flush "struct logcmp_client *client"
.Ft int
.Fn logcmp_stats "struct logcmp_client *client" "struct logcmp_stats *stats"
.Ft void
.Fn logcmp_client_close "struct logcmp_client *client"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library implements
.Dq org.5bsd.log
version
.Dq 1.0.0 .
It connects to the global
.Dq org.5bsd.log
service through
.Xr libservice 3
and prefers a bounded, single-producer
.Xr libshmring 3
record ring.
It falls back to bounded inline records when the provider does not offer a
shared-memory ring.
The provider owns all sink descriptors.
Multiple opens in one process share one reference-counted client, request
sequence, lock, and ring.
The final close detaches the ring and closes the independent global service
session, so a later open starts a clean producer sequence.
.Pp
.Fn logcmp_log
submits a severity, message, and optional newline-separated
.Li KEY=value
fields.
Fields beginning with an underscore are reserved for trusted provider
metadata and are rejected.
Messages and fields are copied into the ring; pointers need not remain valid.
Ring publication performs no per-record control RPC.
The provider drains all available records in batches on a bounded periodic
.Xr kqueue 2
timer, while
.Fn logcmp_flush
provides an explicit synchronous processing boundary.
Ring saturation returns
.Er EAGAIN
and increments the client drop counter.
.Pp
.Fn logcmp_flush
waits until the provider has consumed all records published before the flush
and submitted them to its configured sink.
It does not promise that
.Xr syslogd 8
has written those records to stable storage.
An application requiring crash-stable records needs a typed durable sink
protocol rather than treating ordinary logging as an audit trail.
.Fn logcmp_stats
returns accepted, rejected, and dropped counts and the last accepted sequence.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr libshmring 3 ,
.Xr logcmp 8 ,
.Xr syslogd 8
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
The service label, component instance, receive time, and provider sequence are
trusted metadata obtained from the broker or generated by the provider.
Clients cannot supply reserved fields or sink routing.
Application logging is not an audit trail; security decisions continue to use
OpenBSM.
